.\" ipcrm.1 -- maux's stub for the POSIX ipcrm(1) utility, which
.\" this tree does not provide. An original page (this project's own
.\" text), so it carries no third-party notice -- MIT like the code,
.\" same posture as env.1/man.1. Recorded in docs/POSIX-GAPS.md sec
.\" 5 ("Not applicable, and why") so the omission is not re-
.\" litigated. Rendered at build time to build/man/IPCRM.TXT and
.\" staged on the play image as /usr/man/IPCRM.
.TH IPCRM 1 "September 17, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
ipcrm \- remove a message queue, semaphore set, or shared memory identifier
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ipcrm
is not provided on maux.
maux has no clock-interrupt job scheduler (for at, batch, and
crontab) and no System V interprocess communication (for ipcrm
and ipcs). Its 14-slot round-robin scheduler has no priority
concept for nice and renice to adjust, and the same absence of
scheduling and IPC infrastructure covers fuser and logger.
